\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{The operator domain and real-time evolution}
\date{2026-11-13}

\p{The domain of the Hamiltonian is #{\Dom{H}}. That is the
spelling this Part uses, and #{\extD} is not that domain.
Another printed spelling is #{D(H)}.}

\p{The real-time group generated by a self-adjoint Hamiltonian #{H}
is #{\ue^{-\ui tH}}. Mathematical physics writes #{e^{-itH}}. That
factor of #{\ui} is the one in the unitary group.}
